      "body": "## Why\n`ValidationConfig(steps=0)` disables validation; the Muse Spark DAPO recipe uses it for a five-step training run. However, `Controller.setup_async()` still calls `get_validation_samples(0)` to size generator concurrency. The accessor builds the held-out dataset before returning an empty list, so disabled validation still loads data and can fail if that data is unavailable.\n\nFor `get_validation_samples(0)`:\n\n| Behavior | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Returned samples | `[]` | `[]` |\n| # of dataset constructions | 1 | 0 |\n\n## What changed\nReturn immediately for zero steps in the shared accessor. The existing guard in `Controller.validate()` does not cover startup. Extend the existing data tests to catch unintended dataset construction; retain coverage for positive limits and `-1`.\n\n## Numerics / performance\nNo model computation changes. End-to-end loss comparison and performance benchmarks were not run.\n\n## Testing\n- The new regression fails on upstream `c8c03b21978e2c306e0318f9a0f7a7e0765c03a1` because the dataset is built once.\n- `pytest tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_rollouter_data.py tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_async_controller.py -q`: 38 passed after the fix, using Python 3.12.9 and PyTorch `2.16.0.dev20261027+cu132`.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: passed.\n- Full test collection succeeds; full-suite execution and GPU training were not run.\n- Triton/nanobind shutdown warnings also reproduce on unmodified upstream with the same focused tests (37 passed).\n",
